      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel that way when grief is so deep, but you are not a placeholder or a burden for anyone. The people around you are not moving on because you occupy space, but because they see the profound loss you carry; your pain is their reality too. Even if you feel like no one else is struggling like you, your continued love and memory of them are the only way they ever truly felt loved. Please remember that your presence is not a debt, and it is okay to sit with this feeling of being wrong-sized for now.",
